+# Carbon production bootstrap & validate runbook
+
+This runbook walks through deploying the carbon stack, validating measurement, enforcing budgets, and running a one-click carbon flow.
+
+Prereqs (examples)
+- kubectl/helm configured and CLUSTER_CONTEXT set to target cluster
+- REGISTRY (container registry) set and accessible to cluster nodes
+- COSIGN_KMS_URI set (awskms://alias/... or gcpkms://...)
+- S3_UPLOAD (s3://bucket/path) writable by CI/ops
+- REDIS_URL pointing to Redis (or install via helm)
+- (Optional) ELECTRICITYMAP_API_KEY for region emission factors
+
+1) Deploy stack
+ - export CLUSTER_CONTEXT=<your-kubectl-context>
+ - export REGISTRY=<your-registry>
+ - export REDIS_URL=<redis-url>
+ - kubectl config use-context $CLUSTER_CONTEXT
+ - bash ops/carbon/deploy_stack.sh
+
+2) Validate Redis & webhook
+ - kubectl get pods -n aegis-app
+ - Check webhook logs: kubectl logs deployment/aegis-carbon-webhook -n aegis-app
+
+3) Run the one-click flow
+ - export COSIGN_KMS_URI, S3_UPLOAD
+ - bash ops/carbon/one_click_carbon_flow.sh
+ - Inspect produced artifacts under /tmp/aegis_carbon_demo_*
+
+4) Test budget enforcement (demo)
+ - Seed a namespace budget: redis-cli -u <redis> SET budget:default 0.001
+ - Try to create a Job with annotation aegis/expected_duration_hours > 0.1; webhook will reject if budget exceeded
+
+5) Verify Grafana dashboard
+ - Import ops/monitoring/grafana/carbon_dashboard.json into Grafana
+ - Validate metrics aegis_job_energy_kwh and aegis_job_co2e_kg are visible (or push sample metrics)
+
+6) Operationalize
+ - Add post-job hook in your training launch to call job_carbon_exporter.py
+ - Add carbon audit packager run in your PoA pipeline to produce signed carbon audit bundles
+ - Integrate carbon_aware_scheduler into batch submission flow (Argo/submitter)
+
+Security & production notes
+ - Run webhook with proper TLS certs and configure Kubernetes ValidatingWebhookConfiguration (not created by deploy script).
+ - Do not store COSIGN_KMS_URI or OIDC client secrets in plain files; use Vault or GitHub secrets and OIDC for CI.
+ - Traffic to ElectricityMap must be secured; cache emission factors and avoid DoS.
+
